Subject: [PATCH 138/144] GreatDANE: resolve publisher values with makensis
 -PPO and parse_module_ver (round 4j)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rework the publisher check (test tooling and fixtures only; no product
files). Company and publisher values in greatdane branding.nsi are taken
from makensis -PPO on a wrapper that !includes the branding file and
echoes ${CompanyName} and ${ARPPublisher}. If makensis is missing, the
check FAILs (not PASS).

module.ver is parsed with a vendored copy of Firefox ESR 153.7.0
config/create_rc.py preprocess / parse_module_ver (that file is not in
this snapshot; the source is cited in pepecoin_publisher.py).

Values are normalized (NFKC, casefold, Cyrillic/Greek/Latin-accent
lookalikes, zero-width and non-letters stripped) before matching.
A company or publisher value that contains "pepecoin" or "mozilla" after
that fold is a failure (L8). The official shared.nsh Publisher "Mozilla"
fallback stays, and applies only when ARPPublisher is undefined.

The dead non-publisher / vendor-key path is removed (L9). All 4i fixtures
and the 4j L1–L8 cases NGD reproduced must be rejected; the real tree must
pass.

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
